### 5. Fix validation sequence construction

This is important.

The validation sequences must have access to the previous 60 historical candles as context.

Do NOT create validation sequences using only:

```python
test_dataframe
```

because that produces only approximately:

```text
86 - 60 = 26
```

validation sequences with the current dataset.

Instead:

* Keep the training/validation split chronological.
* Use the last `SEQUENCE_LENGTH` rows from the training dataframe as historical context.
* Concatenate those rows with the validation dataframe.
* Create sequences from the combined dataframe.
* Keep ONLY sequences whose target belongs to the validation period.

Conceptually:

```text
TRAIN DATA
.........................| VALIDATION
                         |
              previous 60 rows
                         ↓
              [60 history + validation]
                         ↓
                 validation sequences
```

This is NOT data leakage because the 60 context rows are historical rows before the validation period.

The validation targets must still come only from the validation period.

Do not allow any validation target to be used as training data.

---

